# Android Manifest — Legacy Havoc-OS Source Baseline

**Purpose:** Historical Android source manifest for initialising and syncing the Havoc-OS-era Android 10 tree.
**Built for:** Android ROM maintainers and build engineers reproducing or researching the legacy source baseline.
**Stage:** Historical reference only. The ten branch pins Android 10.0.0_r40-era sources; it is not an Android 16 baseline or an S20 FE manifest.

---

> **Legacy baseline:** this repository's `ten` branch pins Android 10.0.0_r40 / Havoc-OS-era sources. It is a historical Android 10 manifest, not a current Android 16 build baseline and not an S20 FE ROM manifest. Modernization requires a separate branch with compatible device, vendor and kernel projects.

Havoc-OS
===========


Getting Started
---------------
To get started with the Havoc-OS sources, you'll need to get
familiar with [Git and Repo](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).


Create the Directories
----------------------

You will need to set up some directories in your build environment.

To create them run:

```bash
   mkdir -p ~/bin
   mkdir -p ~/havoc
```

Install the Repository
----------------------

Enter the following to download the "repo" binary and make it executable:

curl https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/git-repo-downloads/repo > ~/bin/repo && chmod a+x ~/bin/repo

You may need to reboot for these changes to take effect.
Now enter the following to initialize the repository:

```bash
   cd ~/havoc
```


To initialize your local repository, use this command:
------------------------------------------------------

```bash
   repo init -u https://github.com/Havoc-OS/android_manifest.git -b ten
```
  
To Sync the source:
----------------

```bash
  repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```


Building the System
---------------

Please note that if you are building on Mac OS X, you are required to install coreutils from MacPorts before you continue.
Initialize the environment with the envsetup.sh script. Note that replacing "source" with a single dot saves a few characters, and the short form is more commonly used in documentation.

```bash
   . build/envsetup.sh
    brunch
```

Enter the number of the build you want to start and press enter


Applying for Maintainership
---------------

If you have successfully built for your device and want to apply for maintainership then drop in a message to SKULSHADY on Telegram or XDA.